## Summary

**Criteria NOT met** — but major progress on the sole blocker (8/tcp `dir_reuse_coherency`). 1/2/4 tcp remain 100%. Marker not written.

**Decisive findings this session (RULE 4):**
1. **Epoch-skip at the drain REFUTED** — a new probe (P34-DRAINEPOCH) proved the loss-block at the release-drain is **current-tenure** (`b_epoch==valid_epoch`), `undestaged`, `comm=rm`. Flags can't distinguish the rare loss from the ~795 legit removes/epoch; the discriminator is *provenance*.
2. **Drain-side graft REFUTED ×2** — built a per-tenure removed-set (`i_dlm_dir_removed`, keyed by inumber) + drain-merge to resolve the peer-add-vs-our-remove ambiguity. It fired surgically (1-2×, not 100s — the removed-set works), but graft creates **cross-disk-block duplicates** (readdir=801) because dedup can't verify global name-uniqueness without reading every disk block. Same wall sess29/33 hit. Abandoned (param default-0).
3. **★ THE FIX (4/5 PASS, was ~50%): new-tenure force-evict + BLI-retire.** `dir_newtenure_evict` force-evicts a stale prior-tenure base at the first modify of a new tenure (cold re-read of the peer's image → normal XFS maintains data+leaf consistency, no graft). sess26 set it default-0 because clearing DONE left a zombie BLI that reflushed stale (readdir=0); **the missing piece was retiring the BLI** (`xfs_buf_item_done`, loss-safe by Invariant-1 at new-tenure). Verified iters 1-4 PASS 8/8, no corruption.

**Residual + last build:** iter 5 failed round 13 with a clean readdir=799 — the new_tenure window only covers the *first* evict-call, so a TRYLOCK-skipped stale base escapes. Built `2EAA0090` (now compiling clean, `dir_newtenure_evict` **default-1**) that adds **per-block** prior-tenure coverage: sync `valid_epoch=cur_mep` once at tenure start, then force-evict+retire any block with `b_epoch < cur_mep` on *any* evict call — catching TRYLOCK-skipped blocks on retry, while never flagging this-tenure work.

**Next session:** deploy `2EAA0090`, run `drc_repro_loop.sh 8 "" 24` bare (default-on) to confirm dir_reuse 8/8 reliably, then bare full `./run.sh {1,2,4,8} tcp` suites for the 100% criteria. Full state in ccmemory `sess34-WIN-newtenure-evict-plus-bli-retire-passes`.

